evidence entity_investigator_0 {
    source: "Agent: entity_investigator (Claude API)"
    summary: "Current market fundamentals show elevated valuations (P/E ~21x vs historical ~16.5x), compressed risk premiums, and profit margins at cyclical highs—conditions historically associated with increased correction risk. While earnings growth expectations remain robust for 2025, sustainability is questionable given margin mean reversion patterns and concentration in mega-cap tech. Interest rate levels (10-year at 4.5%+) create valuation headwinds absent from the 2010s. Leading indicators show stabilization but not strength, with credit markets pricing minimal distress. Base rate analysis suggests 55-65% probability of 15%+ correction within 24 months when fundamentals match current levels, with typical triggers being earnings disappointments, monetary surprises, or exogenous shocks. The probability distribution skews toward fundamental weakness emerging in H2 2025 or 2026 as margin compression and growth deceleration materialize."
    relevance: 0.72p
    date: 2026-03-07
}

