    summary: "AI sector concentration in 2024 exhibits warning signs comparable to historical bubbles (28-30% of S&P 500, elevated valuations, high correlations) but with critical differences: current leaders are highly profitable with strong cash flows, unlike 2000 dot-com. The key vulnerability is the monetization gap—$200B+ annual AI capex generating only $40-60B in attributable revenue currently. Analyst consensus assumes this gap closes by 2026, but if capex fatigue sets in during 2025 without clear ROI, historical precedents suggest 35-55% drawdowns are possible over 12-30 months. The 'soft landing' scenario depends on either: (1) AI revenue realization accelerating to $0.50+ per capex dollar by late 2025, or (2) rest of market rallying to reduce concentration (1987 playbook). Quantifiable trigger points: watch for capex guidance cuts, correlation spikes above 0.80, or earnings revision breadth falling below 50%."
    relevance: 0.78p
    date: 2026-03-07
}

